      "body": "## Summary\n\nPart of #41152.\n\nWith a single KV pool and the default `page_size` 1, `_apply_cuda_graph_metadata` builds the decode page indices but never copies them into `cuda_graph_page_table`. Only the SWA-pool branch and the `page_size > 1` branch do the copy. Unified attention then replays every CUDA-graph decode step against a stale page table and produces garbage from the second generated token on. Eager decode (`--disable-cuda-graph`) builds its own table and is unaffected.\n\n`_transform_table_1_to_real` is a no-op at `page_size` 1, so the fix takes the existing copy branch for every page size.\n\nAffected: any model on the aiter unified path with a single pool and `page_size` 1 under CUDA graphs. That includes Gemma 2/3, whose only aiter decode path is unified attention, and any model forced onto it with `SGLANG_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN=1`.\n\n## Results (1× MI325X, TP1, default CUDA graphs)\n\n8 fixed chat prompts, temperature 0, max 256 tokens, `SGLANG_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN=1`:\n\n| model | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gemma 3 4B | every reply turns to garbage after the first token and runs to 256 tokens | matches triton: reply lengths 84/51/78/39/19/106 vs triton 84/52/78/39/19/106; \"Count from 1 to 20\" identical |\n| Qwen3-8B | garbage (`<think>();++邾ETOELS =~GetInstance…`) | coherent |\n\nGSM8K (lm_eval, temperature 0, strict / flexible):\n\n| model | this PR | reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gemma 3 4B | 0.831 / 0.831 | triton 0.832 / 0.832 |\n| Qwen3-8B | 0.930 / 0.935 | aiter default backend 0.935 / 0.939 |\n\nOn main, GSM8K does not finish on this path because generations never stop.\n\nThree more models, same settings. On main each one answers \"The\" and then produces garbage until the 256-token limit (`The ( ( ( ( …` on Llama 3.1 8B, `The处罚 กลۆ paddock…` on Gemma 3 12B):\n\n| model | reply lengths, this PR | reply lengths, reference | GSM8K this PR | GSM8K reference |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Llama 3.1 8B | 91/76/86/64/8/21/105/256 | identical (aiter default backend) | 0.837 / 0.838 | 0.834 / 0.836 |\n| Gemma 2 9B | 123/78/45/72/15/52/5/246 | 123/77/45/72/15/52/5/252 (triton) | 0.845 / 0.846 | 0.842 / 0.843 |\n| Gemma 3 12B | 256/72/54/79/34/50/95/256 | identical (triton) | 0.933 / 0.933 | 0.933 / 0.932 |\n\n`page_size` > 1 takes the same code path before and after this change. As a control, Qwen3-8B with `--page-size 16` gives the same replies on main and this PR, at the same throughput (1024 in / 512 out at concurrency 4: 580.0 vs 584.4 tok/s; 4096 / 512 at concurrency 32: 1582.7 vs 1609.6 tok/s).\n\nNot fixed here: decode on the unified path is also slow at small batch and long context. Two running requests at about 5K tokens decode at about 11 tok/s on Gemma 3 4B, while triton runs one such request at about 83 tok/s. That is the throughput gap reported in #41152 and needs a separate look.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `test_aiter_unified_graph_page_table.py`: decode replay writes the page table for `page_size` 1 and 16; the `page_size` 1 case fails without this fix\n- [x] End-to-end outputs and GSM8K above: Gemma 3 4B/12B, Gemma 2 9B, Llama 3.1 8B, Qwen3-8B, plus the `page_size` 16 control\n\nFound by [Hyperloom](https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Hyperloom); reviewed and measured by hand.\nHyperloom was optimizing `allenai/Olmo-3-7B-Instruct` (#41012); this bug showed up while checking the same fix on `google/gemma-3-4b-it` (#41143).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36115018685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36115018685)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36115018594](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36115018594)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36115018592](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36115018592)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
